{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Ceuqe3azQosN5kTybYpsG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add a new error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to the ErrorCode enum to represent attempts to confirm a shipment that is not in a confirmable state. This is necessary because the existing codes (SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS) don't represent this case, and the API contract requires machine-readable error codes for client branching logic.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new method `confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): ResponseEntity<Shipment>` annotated with `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")`. The method will:\n   - Retrieve the shipment by ID, throwing ResourceNotFoundException if not found\n   - If status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED and save\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, return as-is (idempotent, no change)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS\n   - Return the shipment with 200 OK status\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four new test cases:\n   - Test confirming a CREATED shipment transitions to CONFIRMED\n   - Test confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds with no change (idempotency)\n   - Test confirming a CANCELLED shipment rejects with 409 and correct error code\n   - Test confirming a non-existent shipment rejects with 404\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n\nI considered reusing an existing error code (e.g., VALIDATION_FAILED) instead of adding a new one. Rejected because:\n- The ticket explicitly requires \"Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API\"\n- Existing patterns use specific error codes for specific failure modes\n- Using VALIDATION_FAILED would be semantically incorrect (the input is valid, the state is invalid)\n- SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS is the clearest contract for clients\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Happy path (CREATED → CONFIRMED):**\n   - Request: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm\n   - Flow: Repository finds shipment with status CREATED → Update to CONFIRMED → Save → Return 200 with updated shipment\n   - Response: `{ \"shipmentId\": \"S-1\", ..., \"status\": \"CONFIRMED\" }`\n\n2. **Idempotent path (CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED):**\n   - Request: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm (when already CONFIRMED)\n   - Flow: Repository finds shipment with status CONFIRMED → Return as-is → Save → Return 200 with unchanged shipment\n   - Response: `{ \"shipmentId\": \"S-1\", ..., \"status\": \"CONFIRMED\" }`\n\n3. **Conflict path (CANCELLED):**\n   - Request: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm (when CANCELLED)\n   - Flow: Repository finds shipment with status CANCELLED → Throw ConflictException → GlobalExceptionHandler catches and returns 409\n   - Response: `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": [] } }`\n\n4. **Not found path:**\n   - Request: POST /shipments/missing/confirm\n   - Flow: Repository findById returns null → Throw ResourceNotFoundException → GlobalExceptionHandler catches and returns 404\n   - Response: `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": [] } }`\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test: \"confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED\"**\n   - Setup: Create a shipment in CREATED status\n   - Action: POST to /shipments/{id}/confirm\n   - Verify: Status 200, returned shipment has status CONFIRMED\n\n2. **Test: \"idempotently succeeds when confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment\"**\n   - Setup: Create and confirm a shipment\n   - Action: POST to /shipments/{id}/confirm again\n   - Verify: Status 200, returned shipment still has status CONFIRMED, no error\n\n3. **Test: \"rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with error envelope\"**\n   - Setup: Create a shipment and manually set its status to CANCELLED in the repository\n   - Action: POST to /shipments/{id}/confirm\n   - Verify: Status 409 Conflict, error code is SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS\n\n4. **Test: \"rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with 404\"**\n   - Setup: No shipment created\n   - Action: POST to /shipments/missing/confirm\n   - Verify: Status 404, error code is SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nLet me implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":508,"cache_read_input_tokens":20181,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":508},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fbc76bb5-db93-4a17-a250-0effd22f613a","uuid":"72e8df6c-13a9-40c7-bea2-1aff51d845d5","timestamp":"2026-09-10T13:29:59.269Z","request_id":"req_011Ceuqe2jeMsx7x23gUwqG5"}
