because the confirm endpoint needs a specific error code to distinguish \"invalid shipment state\" from \"not found\" errors. The code follows existing naming conventions (ErrorCode enum values). This was required.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added `confirm()` method as a POST endpoint at `/{shipmentId}/confirm`. The method:\n   - Fetches the shipment (throws ResourceNotFoundException if missing)\n   - Applies state transition logic: CREATED→CONFIRMED, CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED (idempotent), CANCELLED→ConflictException\n   - Saves and returns with 200 OK\n   - Uses exactly the error patterns already in the file. This was required.\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added 4 new test methods covering all cases:\n   - Happy path: CREATED → CONFIRMED\n   - Idempotent: CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED\n   - Conflict: CANCELLED → 409 with error code\n   - Not found: Missing ID → 404 with error code\n   - All tests follow existing patterns (MockMvc, jsonPath assertions, status checks). This was required.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All ticket requirements are implemented and verified.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement   Add a POST endpoint to confirm a shipment, transitioning it from CREATED to CONFIRMED with idempotent behavior for retries, and appropriate error handling for invalid states and missing resources.\n\nChanged       ApiError.kt: Added SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS error code enum value to support invalid shipment state conflicts.\n              ShipmentController.kt: Added confirm() method to POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm, implementing state transition logic with idempotency and error handling.\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt: Added 4 new test cases covering confirm operation for CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED, and missing shipment cases.\n\nTests         \"confirms a CREATED shipment and transitions it to CONFIRMED\" — validates happy path with status transition and response body.\n              \"idempotently succeeds when confirming 